    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1295">

                <pb facs="0884" n="768" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg768"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/10533.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Edwards to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Acapulco</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-01-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 12, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mariscal has entered Acapulco with 300 men asking for money and ammunition. The
                    military commander made forced loans yesterday in order to raise money to pay
                    the former’s troops including the Americans in his demands and threatening that
                    Mariscal would not wait. There is great apprehension of trouble and the garrison
                    is entirely insufficient to afford protection. Embassy advised.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwards</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
